    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMMON MISTAKES\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#C62828",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Assuming an in-memory background task is durable or retried; its work is lost if the process stops.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "title": "Practical tip",
      "text": "Keep `BackgroundTasks` for short work and tell the client what was accepted in the response."
    },
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "title": "One level deeper",
      "text": "A separate worker queue can add retries, monitoring, and throttling for long work; `BackgroundTasks` does not provide these automatically."
    },
    {
      "type": "warning",
      "title": "Important warning",
      "text": "Do not rely on an in-process callback for critical email, payments, or work that must not be lost."
    },
